---
import Presentation from "../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Session 5: Makerspace Safety II</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Session 5</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Makerspace Safety II</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>You Named Your Tool</h2>
              <p>
                Last session, you looked back at your concept sketches and
                named the specific tool or machine yours depends on most.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Today, you get certified on it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>From Awareness to Certification</h2>
              <p>
                Session 4 was about recognizing hazards across the whole
                shop.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>From Awareness to Certification</h2>
              <p>
                Today is about being <b class="text-sn-theme"
                  >actually cleared</b
                > to use specific tools on your own, not just recognizing
                that they're dangerous.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Format</h2>
              <ol>
                <li class="fragment">Your instructor demonstrates each tool you'll need</li>
                <li class="fragment">You practice under direct supervision</li>
                <li class="fragment">You take a certification quiz on today's protocols</li>
              </ol>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>The Certification Quiz</h2>
              <p>Passing score: <b class="text-sn-theme">100%.</b></p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>The Certification Quiz</h2>
              <p>
                Repeatable until you pass. 100% isn't a punishment &mdash;
                it's the standard, because partial safety knowledge isn't
                safe knowledge.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">Certification is per-tool, not blanket.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Passing today clears you on what was demonstrated today. Need
                a new tool later this semester? You get shown that one too,
                the same way.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">Watching isn't the same as doing.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                You're not cleared until you've practiced it yourself, under
                supervision &mdash; not just seen it done once.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Next Time</h2>
              <p>Session 6: Caliper Use &amp; Precision</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                From staying safe in the shop to measuring precisely once
                you're in it.
              </p>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <h3>Step 1: Tool Demonstrations</h3>
          <p>
            Your instructor will demonstrate each tool or machine you'll need
            access to this semester. Watch the full demonstration before
            attempting anything yourself.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 2: Supervised Practice</h3>
          <p>
            Under your instructor's direct supervision, practice the specific
            safe-use steps for each tool demonstrated.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 3: Record Your Protocol Notes</h3>
          <p>For each tool demonstrated, write down:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The tool's name</li>
            <li>The <b class="text-sn-theme">one non-negotiable rule</b> for using it</li>
            <li>What to do if something goes wrong</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Step 4: Certification Quiz</h3>
          <p>
            A quiz on today's protocols, administered by your instructor.
            Passing score is <b class="text-sn-theme">100%</b>, and it's
            repeatable until you get there &mdash; this isn't about a single
            attempt, it's about actually knowing the protocol before you're
            cleared to use the tool alone.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Before you're cleared to use any tool independently, all three must be true:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>You watched the full demonstration for that tool</li>
            <li>You practiced it under direct supervision</li>
            <li>You passed the certification quiz at 100%</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Missing any one of these means you're not cleared yet &mdash;
            that's not a technicality, it's the actual standard.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer the following questions before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>
              Pick one tool demonstrated today. What's the one non-negotiable
              rule for using it safely?
            </li>
            <li>
              Why do you think the passing standard for this quiz is 100%
              instead of something like 80%?
            </li>
            <li>
              Session 6 introduces calipers, a precision measurement tool.
              Is precision measurement itself ever a safety issue, or is it
              purely about design quality?
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit your protocol notes and your reflection.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
